{
  "_comment": [
    "Template only, and named so Codex cannot mistake it for the real thing.",
    "`agentgit install` writes hooks.json beside it, with the NODE and TRACK",
    "placeholders replaced by absolute paths on this machine. Codex performs no",
    "command substitution and does not resolve a POSIX-style relative script path",
    "on Windows, so absolute paths are the only form that works everywhere. That is",
    "why hooks.json is gitignored and this template is not.",
    "",
    "Matchers are deliberately broad. The hook script classifies the tool itself",
    "and ignores anything that cannot change a file, so a tool Codex renames or",
    "adds still gets recorded instead of silently dropping out of the ledger."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ]
  }
}
